# Response headers for the Cloudflare Pages deployment.
#
# The site is static, has no accounts, no cookies and no user-generated content,
# so this is defence in depth rather than a fix for a known hole. It matters
# mostly because the app does render trusted HTML (Learn article bodies) and
# JSON-LD, and because a reference tool people are asked to trust should not be
# framable or sniffable.
#
# `script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'`: the pre-paint theme bootstrap in
# app.html is an inline script, and SvelteKit emits inline hydration data.
# 'unsafe-inline' is therefore load-bearing until those are nonce-based.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
